+# ACP Release Gate
+
+This document governs publication from `Homelab/ACP`. It complements the
+canonical release-management policy in `yeraziael/ai-governance`; it does not
+weaken that policy.
+
+## Release Is A Separate State
+
+A merged pull request, a green pull-request run, and a version string ending in
+`-draft` are implementation evidence. None creates a release. A release exists
+only when an immutable annotated Git tag and a published Gitea release refer to
+the same full commit SHA.
+
+## Blocking Gates
+
+Before creating a tag, the release owner MUST verify all of the following on
+the intended commit:
+
+1. The release-preparation PR is independently reviewed, merged, and its
+   required Gitea Actions run is green.
+2. `VERSION` is a stable Semantic Version without a `-draft` suffix and equals
+   the proposed tag without its `v` prefix.
+3. `CHANGELOG.md`, every current-version specification, schema description, and
+   release notes name the same version. Historical specifications retain their
+   historical version.
+4. `python3 SCHEMAS/test_schemas.py` passes on the exact target commit.
+5. The exact full SHA, CI run URL or ID, independent review, release notes,
+   compatibility impact, rollback path, and runtime-consumer status are
+   recorded as durable release evidence.
+6. A post-merge audit has no unresolved blocking finding. Follow-ups from older
+   audits must be re-checked rather than copied forward.
+7. The release-evidence format can bind the tag and its peeled commit without
+   a self-referential commit-SHA claim. The current cross-repository policy
+   needs an explicit resolution for this format before ACP's first stable
+   release.
+
+## Publication And Verification
+
+1. Create the annotated `vMAJOR.MINOR.PATCH` tag only after all gates pass.
+2. Publish the Gitea release from that tag, never from `main` or another moving
+   branch.
+3. Re-read the tag object, peeled commit, release target, title, notes, and
+   assets. Record the result in the release evidence.
+4. Confirm every declared runtime consumer is pinned to the released version or
+   is explicitly documented as using a draft. A runtime skill checksum alone is
+   not a protocol release pin.
+5. A defect after publication requires a corrective version. Published tags and
+   releases are never moved, deleted, or overwritten.
+
+## Automation Requirements
+
+The protected CI contract must reject a version/documentation mismatch. A
+post-publication release-audit job must authenticate to Gitea and fail when a
+stable tag lacks a published release, when the release target differs from the
+peeled tag commit, or when release notes are empty. This job is intentionally
+not enabled until its least-privilege credential and the evidence-binding
+format are defined and reviewed.
