+# ACP Release-State Audit, 2026-07-25
+
+## Scope And Evidence
+
+This audit is based on the canonical `Homelab/ACP` Git history and Gitea API,
+the `yeraziael/ai-governance` canonical-governance repository and GitHub
+mirror, and the Slarti OpenCode runtime. It distinguishes an immutable Git tag
+from a hosting-platform release and from a draft version in a working tree.
+
+## Version Inventory
+
+| Version | Commit | Tag | Gitea release | Status |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| `0.1.0-draft` | `d7933eb9564b55105bd61946f867496d2dc66f53` | `v0.1.0-draft` (annotated) | Published prerelease `v0.1.0-draft`, targeted at `main` | Published draft prerelease; target must be verified by peeled tag, not branch text |
+| `0.2.0-draft` | `beca7ca1db33794510771f5d9c5db1e4e0a17eea` | None | None | Implemented in merged ACP PR #6; never published |
+| `0.3.0-draft` | `99ce7eeea61022357c935eb6e2af061bafe30944` | None | None | Review-provenance implementation merged in ACP PR #9; never published |
+| `0.3.0-draft` current main | `07c3fcbd0f53493b847d812eede1df68770f84c2` | None | None | Includes post-v0.3 audit and immutable-identity fixes; Gitea CI run 686 failed in `schema-tests` |
+
+No `v0.2.0`, `v0.3.0`, or later ACP tag exists. No stable ACP Gitea release
+exists. There are no open ACP release PRs at the audit point.
+
+## Merge History Relevant To Release State
+
+| PR | Merge commit | Meaning |
+|---|---|---|
+| ACP #6 | `beca7ca1db33794510771f5d9c5db1e4e0a17eea` | Execution and Trigger Contracts (`0.2.0-draft`) |
+| ACP #7 | `cf48b82dcf53c144ae8369eb7f37b7b196875d3d` | v0.2 review fixes, merged into its feature branch rather than `main` |
+| ACP #9 | `99ce7eeea61022357c935eb6e2af061bafe30944` | Review Provenance (`0.3.0-draft`) |
+| ACP #10 | `682071a0e9fddc0e8dc3ec8ec7291133e864ed5a` | Post-merge audit |
+| ACP #8 | `07c3fcbd0f53493b847d812eede1df68770f84c2` | Immutable-identity correction now on `main` |
+
+The post-merge audit at `682071a` is stale: it says ACP #8 remains open and
+the `github-review` skill still needs an ACP v0.3 update. ACP #8 was later
+merged at `07c3fcb`; `yeraziael/ai-governance` main at
+`de1a9f972a15e26229a938bf72c582df88e6a5f8` contains the ACP v0.3 skill
+upgrade, and the runtime copy has the identical SHA-256 checksum.
+
+## Cross-System Comparison
+
+| Surface | Observed state | Consistency |
+|---|---|---|
+| Canonical ACP Git/Gitea | `main` declares `0.3.0-draft`; only `v0.1.0-draft` tag and prerelease are published | Incomplete release state |
+| ACP documentation | README describes release binding but did not distinguish a draft working version from a published release; changelog places v0.2.1 fixes inside the v0.3 draft entry | Ambiguous until this audit and gate were added |
+| Governance repository | GitHub and canonical Gitea `ai-governance` both resolve `main` to `de1a9f9`; `v0.1.0` and `v0.2.0` tags exist | Git mirrors agree on commits and tags |
+| Governance releases | GitHub has stable releases for v0.1.0 and v0.2.0; the committed v0.2 evidence names `cac16fe`, while the annotated tag peels to `fc9e644`. The Gitea release endpoint for `yeraziael/ai-governance` returned HTTP 404 to the Slarti audit credential, so its release inventory is not asserted here. | GitHub evidence/tag mismatch; Gitea release state requires an authorized re-check |
+| GitHub ACP mirror | No `Homelab/ACP` or `yeraziael/ACP` GitHub repository was accessible with the audit credential | No GitHub ACP mirror is evidenced; it must not be assumed |
+| Runtime | `~/.opencode/skills/github-review/SKILL.md` is byte-identical to `ai-governance/skills/github-review.md` at `de1a9f9` and declares ACP v0.3 support | Skill content is synchronized, but it is not version-pinned to an ACP release |
+
+## Gap Analysis
+
+1. ACP v0.2 was merged and tested at `beca7ca`, but was never tagged or
+   released. Subsequent review findings and immutable-identity corrections mean
+   it is not an appropriate first stable baseline.
+2. ACP v0.3 was merged and its initial CI run was green at `99ce7ee`, but it
+   lacks a tag and release. The current `main` CI run fails before executing the
+   suite because its workflow performs an unpinned runtime dependency install.
+3. `VERSION`, changelog, and specifications use draft markers, while the README
+   previously implied that a current release existed. A draft version cannot be
+   treated as a release.
+4. The current `CONFORMANCE/post-merge-v0.3.md` carries follow-ups that are now
+   resolved, so it cannot serve as final release evidence without a refreshed
+   audit.
+5. The canonical governance release policy requires committed evidence to name
+   the full tag target, while also requiring the tag to point at the merged
+   release-prep commit containing that evidence. A commit cannot contain its own
+   final SHA; the governance v0.2 evidence demonstrates the resulting mismatch.
+6. No CI job currently verifies Gitea release existence or release-to-tag target
+   equality after publication. Enabling one needs a reviewed least-privilege
+   credential and a settled evidence model.
+
+## Decision Recommendation
+
+Do not retroactively publish ACP v0.2. Its original implementation was followed
+by review corrections and the current main branch contains them only as part of
+the v0.3 draft line. Publishing it now would create a stable release known to
+exclude later correctness work.
+
+Prepare and publish **ACP v0.3.0 as the first stable ACP release** only after:
+
+1. this branch's CI dependency fix is merged and a Gitea Actions run on its
+   exact merge commit is green;
+2. the governance evidence-binding contradiction has an approved, implementable
+   resolution;
+3. a release-preparation PR changes the intended stable version consistently,
+   refreshes the post-merge audit against its exact target, and records complete
+   release notes and runtime-consumer status;
+4. the tag and Gitea release are created and independently re-read.
+
+## Required Governance Hardening
+
+1. Treat merge, CI success, tag creation, release publication, and runtime
+   deployment as distinct states with separately recorded gates.
+2. Require a release checklist and a post-merge audit that expires when any
+   recorded follow-up changes state.
+3. Make release evidence satisfiable: bind the release to the peeled annotated
+   tag in a post-publication attestation, or store the immutable target in an
+   external release record. Do not require a commit to contain its own SHA.
+4. Add protected CI version-drift checks and a post-publication Gitea audit for
+   missing releases, missing notes, and tag/release target disagreement.
+5. Require runtime consumers to record the released ACP tag and commit they
+   implement. A content checksum verifies synchronization only; it does not
+   establish a release deployment.
